cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Resolving Zero-Inflation in Bandgap Prediction for High-Throughput Materials Discovery using a Memory-Efficient, Consumer-Hardware Machine Learning Framework"

message: "If you use this software, please cite the associated research article and this software release."

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Tyagi"
    given-names: "Devansh"

version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-30"

abstract: >
  Source code implementing a machine-learning hurdle
  framework for inorganic materials bandgap prediction using Materials
  Project data. The repository includes the complete prediction pipeline,
  evaluation against a more recent Materials Project release, and
  CPU-versus-GPU benchmarking and analysis.

keywords:
  - bandgap prediction
  - Materials Project
  - machine learning
  - materials informatics
  - XGBoost
  - GPU acceleration
  - hurdle model
  - conformal prediction
  - uncertainty quantification

repository-code: "https://github.com/devanshtyagi26/Bandgap-Hurdle-Framework"

license: "MIT"
